{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789247106,"nonce":"KvZWkYztUb5OOSO2+62YY0jaaWY=","title":"A fiber def's arguments never reach its body","message":"A call to a `fiber def` lowers to `FiberNew` with the function's address\nand nothing else; the body is entered by the runtime with no arguments,\nso its parameters hold whatever the registers held. `fiber def g(n: i64)`\nyields garbage for `n`, and every existing fiber test uses parameterless\nfibers.\n\nThe runtime now carries an environment per fiber (`krio_fiber_new_with_env`\nstores one, `krio_fiber_env` returns the running fiber's), which is how\nthe Python frontend hands a generator its arguments and captured cells\nthrough a body that takes no parameters. The compiler-level fix for\nZynML's `fiber def` with parameters is to do the same in the SSA: build\nthe environment at the call site, and have the body's prologue read its\nparameters from `krio_fiber_env`.","files":null}]}